# VS-13 S1.1 (2026-05-04, addresses PR #73 review by Copilot bot):
#
# `engines.node: ">=22.0.0"` in package.json is ADVISORY by default —
# npm prints a warning but still installs on Node 20. PR #73 review
# correctly flagged that this didn't actually enforce the Node 22 floor.
#
# `engine-strict=true` makes `npm install` fail outright when the
# running Node doesn't match `engines`. Combined with CI's
# `actions/setup-node@v4` pinning Node 22, this turns the floor from
# advisory into hard enforcement.
#
# Local devs hitting this on Node 20 should `nvm use 22` (or run
# `node --version` to confirm). Error message points to engines field.
engine-strict=true
